I propose to take Questions Nos. 588 and 589 together.
The Temporary Protection Transition Scheme opened for applications on 30 September 2026.
Applicants must meet a number of eligibility criteria under the published policy, including having resided in Ireland as a Beneficiary of Temporary Protection for at least one year prior to 30 September 2026 and being resident in independent accommodation at the time of application.
An applicant must demonstrate that they have been in employment or self-employment for at least six months immediately prior to the opening date of the Scheme, with average gross annual earnings of €29,432, and must continue to be in employment both at the date of application and at the date a decision is made on their application.
The average gross earnings will be considered through an assessment of all the evidence provided by an applicant. Under Section 6 of the Scheme, all applicants are required to submit a minimum of two of the following documents in relation to employment which cover the period 30 March 2026 – 30 September 2026:
• At least 4 previous payslips;
• Contract of employment or a letter from their employer confirming employment details;
• Revenue records;
• Bank statements;
• Employment Detail Summary or Statement of Liability;
Where a contracted annual salary is not available or a person can only show income evidence for the minimum 6 months of employment required, they must demonstrate that their average gross earnings would reach €29,4

