Progressing the implementation of the Action Plan for Insurance Reform 2025–2029 to further strengthen the insurance sector in Ireland is a key priority for Government. The Action Plan sets out a number of priority actions, focused on areas where the greatest impact on the transparency, affordability and availability of insurance can be achieved.
The Action Plan is also subject to regular oversight through the Cabinet Sub-Group on Insurance Reform, which I chair. The Sub-Group provides a “whole-of-Government” approach to drive the Action Plan forward and consider the progress that each Minister is making in implementing the specific actions for which they have responsibility. This work is also supported at official level by a Senior Officials Group. The Sub-Group meets periodically to review progress and has met on a number of occasions since it was re-established in April 2025 and is scheduled to meet again at the end of this month.
